  abstract = {Lercanidipine, a dihydropyridine calcium channel blocker, and enalapril, an ACE inhibitor, are established antihypertensive agents. A fixed-dose tablet  formulation of lercanidipine/enalapril is approved in Germany for the treatment  of hypertension in patients not responding to monotherapy.  Lercanidipine/enalapril 10mg/10mg once daily significantly reduced sitting  diastolic blood pressure and sitting systolic blood pressure, relative to  lercanidipine 10mg once daily, in a 12-week, randomised, double-blind trial in  patients with mild to moderate hypertension who had previously not responded to 4  weeks' treatment with lercanidipine. In a similarly designed trial,  lercanidipine/enalapril 10mg/20mg once daily was significantly more effective  than enalapril 20mg once daily in hypertensive patients who had previously not  responded to enalapril monotherapy. Fixed-dose lercanidipine/enalapril was  generally well tolerated, with a tolerability profile similar to that of either  of the individual drugs alone or placebo. Cough was reported in},
