  pages = {53--58},
  location = {France},
  issn = {0035-2640},
  abstract = {Owing to its original pharmacokinetic profile, lisinopril can be taken once a day, independently of meals, providing a 24-hour inhibition of the  angiotensin-converting enzyme. Lisinopril is a potent angiotensin-converting  enzyme inhibitor. Administered in doses of 2.5 to 20 mg per day, it improves the  functional and haemodynamic state of patients whose congestive heart failure is  refractory to the digitalis-diuretic treatment. The drug is well tolerated, and  no severe side-effects have been reported. Lisinopril seems to be at least as  effective as captopril in congestive heart failure, and it has over the latter  the advantage of a once a day dosage therapy.},
