  issn = {0043-5147},
  abstract = {In the paper general remarks concerning ACE-inhibitors (especially enalapril) use in children have been described. Kidney artery stenosis, hypovolemia, and shock  are only ones contraindications to this treatment in a childhood, even in the  first period after birth. Anyhow, it was stressed on the basis of literature that  at a beginning of extrauterine life the kinetics of these drugs is changed, thus  they should be recommended carefully and in low doses. It was stressed, as well,  that up to now appeared only a few papers concerning ACE-inhibitors use a  childhood. It is suggested that enalapril can be used as an rather safety drug in  pediatric patients suffering from circulatory insufficiency or arterial  hypertension.},
