  abstract = {Overdose with angiotensin-converting enzyme (ACE) inhibitors is still a relatively underreported phenomenon. We report here a case of an unintentional  overdose of enalapril (100 mg) together with other medications. The patient  experienced no adverse consequences. Pharmacokinetic evaluation revealed a t 1/2  for enalaprilat (prodrug) of seven hours and for enalapril at 36 hours. Based on  this case report as well as others, guidelines for assessment and treatment of  these patients are proposed. Management of hypotension is the primary therapeutic  intervention.},
